[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m uint8_t threshold = (param1 > 0 && param1 <= 255) ? (uint8_t)param1 : 3;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m With `n` distinct input bytes the length becomes `2n`, and the C writes all `2n`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m bytes through the 256-byte array. For `n > 128` that is a stack buffer overflow.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
