I chose not to emulate this, which is the one judgment call worth your review. Reproducing it means hard-coding one compiler's frame layout: the [38;5;10m-O2[0m build segfaults at the same input where [38;5;10m-O0[0m exits 0 with wrong bytes, so there is no single right answer to match, and producing exit 139 from safe Rust would mean raising SIGSEGV artificially. The 512-byte backing buffer matches the C everywhere its behavior is defined. [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m documents this with the measured boundary table.[0m[0m
